SUMMARY:🔥🌅 GOODBYE SUMMER\, HELLO FALL: TORONTO ISLAND BONFIRE 🌅
 🔥
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🔥
 🌅 GOODBYE SUMMER\, HELLO FALL: TORONTO ISLAND BONFIRE 🌅🔥\n\n### F
 ire\, Food\, Music & One Last Summer Night by the Lake\n\nSummer has to en
 d eventually — so why not send it off properly?\nJoin us on **Toronto Is
 land** for an evening bonfire at Olympic Island as we say goodbye to summe
 r and welcome the beginning of fall.\nWe’ll take the ferry across togeth
 er\, settle in by the fire\, enjoy some food and music\, roast marshmallow
 s\, and spend the evening relaxing by the water with the Toronto skyline i
 n the background.\n\nThis isn't a walk.\nIt isn't a tour.\n\nIt's a **soci
 al evening designed to give us time to actually sit around\, talk\, laugh\
 , eat\, and connect with one another.**\nWhether you've been coming to the
  group for years or this is your first event\, this is a chance to slow do
 wn and enjoy the people around you.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **Wha
 tsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrK
 Anc)**\n\n## 🔥 THE PLAN\n\nWe'll meet at the ferry terminal and take th
 e ferry together to Toronto Island.\nOnce we arrive\, we'll make our way o
 ver to **Olympic Island**\, where our fire pit will be waiting.\n\nWe'll h
 ave:\n🔥 A bonfire\n🌭 Hot dogs — including vegetarian options\n🍡
  Marshmallows for roasting\n🎶 Music\n🌆 Beautiful views of the Toront
 o skyline\n🗣️ Plenty of time to sit\, talk and socialize\nThe goal is
  simple:\n**Come for the fire.**\n**Stay for the food.**\n\n**Leave with a
  few more people you know.** 🔥💛\n\n## 🚢 FERRY INFORMATION — PLE
 ASE READ\n\nThe **fall ferry schedule has not been released yet**\, so the
  ferry departure and return times listed below are **subject to change**.\
 nI will update the event as soon as the official fall schedule is availabl
 e.\n\n### Current tentative schedule:\n\n📍 **Meetup:** 5:00 PM\n🚢 **
 Ferry:** Approximately 5:20 PM\n🔥 **Bonfire:** Olympic Island\n🚢 **R
 eturn ferry:** Approximately 9:00 PM\n\n**Please do not make other plans a
 round these ferry times until the fall schedule has been confirmed.**\n\nO
 nce the schedule is released\, the event page will be updated with the exa
 ct times.\n\n## 🧢 MEETUP DETAILS\n\n📍 **Inside the Jack Layton Ferry
  Terminal\, near the bathrooms**\nYou must enter the ferry terminal and ha
 ve your ferry ticket **scanned before entering the waiting area**.\nOnce y
 ou're inside the terminal\, head toward the **bathrooms**.\n🫎 I'll be w
 earing my Moose Hat.\n\n**PLEASE BE ON TIME.**\n\nThe ferry will not wait 
 for us\, and I will not be able to hold up the group while waiting for lat
 e arrivals.\n\n## 🎟️ FERRY TICKET\n\nYou are responsible for purchasi
 ng your own ferry ticket.\n**Ferry fare:** To be confirmed once the fall s
 chedule and current fare are released.\n\n👉 **[Click Here for Ferry Tic
 kets](https://secure.toronto.ca/FerryTicketOnline/tickets2/index.jsp)**\n\
 n# 💵 MEETUP FEE — PLEASE READ BEFORE RSVPING\n\nThe meetup fee for th
 is event is **$10**.\nPayment must be made by **e-transfer to:**\n📧 **m
 athewmaclean@hotmail.com**\n\n### Payment is required within 24 hours of s
 igning up.\n\nThis applies to **everyone**.\n\nIt does not matter whether 
 you have been a member for one week\, one year\, or ten years. It does not
  matter whether you are a long-standing member or a member in good standin
 g.\n**Everyone attending this event pays the $10 meetup fee.**\nThere are 
 no exceptions.\n\nYour payment helps cover:\n🔥 Fire permit\n🪵 Firewo
 od\n🌭 Hot dogs and buns\n🍡 Marshmallows\n🎶 Music\n🥄 Shared roa
 sting supplies\n\n**If payment is not received within 24 hours\, your RSVP
  will be removed so someone else can take the spot.**\n\n## ⚠️ RSVP CO
 MMITMENT\n\nPlease only RSVP if you genuinely intend to attend.\n\n**When 
 you sign up\, you must also answer all of the event questions.**\nThis inf
 ormation helps me plan the food\, fire and logistics for the evening.\n\nP
 lease don't RSVP simply because the event looks interesting and then decid
 e later whether you feel like coming.\n\nIf you aren't sure you can attend
 \, **please wait until you know before signing up.**\n\nOnce you've commit
 ted\, please respect that commitment.\n\n## 🍴 WHAT YOUR $10 INCLUDES\n\
 nYour meetup fee includes:\n\n*City permit and fire-related costs\n- Firew
 ood\n*Hot dogs and buns\n- Vegetarian hot dog option\n*Sauces and condimen
 ts\n- Marshmallows\n*Music\n- Shared roasting sticks\n\n**Bring your own d
 rinks.**\n\n## 🎒 WHAT TO BRING\n\n🥤 Your own drinks\n\n🪑 Folding 
 chair or blanket\n🧥 A sweater or jacket — September evenings can get 
 cool\n🍪 Something small to share if you'd like\n🎲 **A game to share*
 * — bring one along if you'd like and feel free to get a group together 
 to play\n🔥 Your own roasting stick if you have one\n📱 Your phone/cam
 era\nDogs are welcome as long as they are well behaved and permitted in th
 e area.\n\n## 🌧️ WEATHER\n\nThis event is planned as an outdoor bonfi
 re and will happen in most weather conditions.\nIf severe weather or unsaf
 e conditions make the event impossible\, the event may be cancelled or res
 cheduled.\nPlease keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n## 🌈 TH
 E POINT OF THE EVENING\n\nThis is a social event.\nThe bonfire is really j
 ust the **container**.\nThe important part is what happens around it — s
 itting together\, talking to someone you've never met\, catching up with p
 eople you already know\, sharing food\, laughing\, and maybe making a conn
 ection that continues long after the fire goes out.\nThat's what this grou
 p is really about.\n\nWe also organize:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n
 🎭 Arts & culture\n🍽️ Restaurant outings\n🎉 Social events\nThere
 's always something happening.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? P
 ost on the event wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.co
 m**\n\n### 🔥 Come for the bonfire.\n\n### 🌭 Stay for the food.\n\n##
 # 🌅 Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.\n\n**Let's 
 give summer the send-off it deserves.** 💛🔥
